---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { APP_STORE_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL, pathFor } from '../../config/site';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Website privacy notice"
  description="How Golden Moments' static website handles browsing, hosting logs, email support, and the interactive picture preview. Separate from the mobile app policy."
>
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Golden Moments / Website</p>
      <h1>Website privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="interior-lede">You can explore this website without signing in or handing over your photographs.</p>
      <p class="small-print"><time datetime="2026-10-18">Updated October 18, 2026</time> · Website only</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="reading-column prose-page">
    <section class="legal-summary" aria-labelledby="website-summary">
      <h2 id="website-summary">At a glance</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't run visitor accounts, advertising pixels, analytics scripts, or an online photo uploader on this website.</li>
        <li>The small matching example uses illustrations supplied with the site and does not save a personal game history.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages hosts the site</strong> and may process ordinary connection details as part of delivering it.</li>
        <li>If you email us, we receive your address and whatever you choose to send.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <h2>1. Who operates this website?</h2>
    <p>Cloudjet Solutions Pte. Ltd., Singapore, publishes the Golden Moments website. For privacy or support inquiries, contact <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. This notice is specifically for the <strong>website</strong>. The <a href={pathFor('/app-privacy/')}>mobile app privacy policy</a> covers Golden Moments on iPhone and iPad.</p>

    <h2>2. Browsing and the example game</h2>
    <p>The website is a static collection of pages. Its own code does not use visitor analytics, advertising trackers, or cookies to track you, and it does not run a backend account or photo-storage service. The illustrated matching activity runs in your browser. It doesn't request your Photos library, upload files, or keep your play history after the page closes.</p>
    <p>You can adjust browser zoom or use assistive technology without registering or sending details to us.</p>

    <h2>3. Hosting and technical data</h2>
    <p>GitHub Pages delivers the site. Like other web hosts, GitHub may handle IP addresses, requested URLs, browser or device information, timestamps, and security logs as part of serving and protecting the pages. These hosting records are managed by GitHub; we do not have a website analytics dashboard that profiles visitors. Read <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a> for its data practices.</p>
    <p>Links to Apple's App Store, external caregiving information, and email open separate services. Those services may collect their own information under their published policies.</p>

    <h2>4. When you contact us</h2>
    <p>Sending us email shares your address, message, and any attachments you include with us and the email services involved. We use this information to respond, address a privacy or rights concern, and satisfy applicable obligations. We retain correspondence only as long as reasonably necessary for those purposes or required by law; we review records for deletion when no longer needed.</p>
    <p>For your privacy, please do not send photos of relatives, diagnoses, patient files, identity documents, or payment details just to ask for routine help.</p>

    <h2>5. Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can leave this website without creating an account or deleting a site profile; none is created by us. For information you voluntarily emailed, you may request access, correction, deletion, or other rights where applicable by contacting <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL + '?subject=Golden%20Moments%20website%20privacy'}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. We may need to verify authorization and may keep information when law requires it.</p>
    <p>Requests involving information managed solely by Apple, GitHub, your browser, or email providers must also be directed to the relevant provider.</p>

    <h2>6. Children, locations, and changes</h2>
    <p>The website is designed for older adults, families, and caregivers, not directed to children under 13. We do not operate a child's account or ask visitors to provide health information. Hosting and email providers may process data outside Singapore subject to applicable laws.</p>
    <p>We may change this notice if the website's features or practices change, and will update the date shown above. We do not treat a changed notice as permission for previously undisclosed collection.</p>

    <h2>About the mobile app</h2>
    <p>Only this notice covers website browsing. The <a href={pathFor('/app-privacy/')}>mobile app privacy policy</a> explains the app's local picture activities, optional photos in versions that support them, device backups, and third-party software. The <a href={APP_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">App Store listing</a> describes the currently published version.</p>
    <p class="back-home"><a class="text-link" href={pathFor('/legal/')}>← All legal information</a></p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
